# LOAD-BEARING. Five lines that prevent a crash-loop.
#
# The SQL migrations are applied verbatim and checksummed. On a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true (this one, local AND system), git would hand the working tree
# CRLF copies, the checksums would then disagree with the LF-recorded rows in an
# existing database, and the server would crash-loop on boot. That has happened
# once already, in an earlier version of this project.
#
# The upstream pin said `migrations/*.sql`. This repo keeps them in `sql/`, so the
# path is changed to match: a pin that names the wrong directory is not a pin.
sql/*.sql text eol=lf
# MADE THE SAME MISTAKE TWICE: the divergence migrations live in sql_meshychat/ and the
# pin above does not cover them. git reported 'LF will be replaced by CRLF' on the first
# one. A pin that names the wrong directory is not a pin.
sql_meshychat/*.sql text eol=lf
# The down scripts beside them (divergence 039): psql applies them, and a CRLF copy would
# differ from the text the tests compare against.
sql_meshychat/down/*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/context_v1/*.jsonl -text
